    <changeSet id="20260828100000-36-backfill-plagiarism-case-post-author" author="krusche">
        <comment>
            The continuous plagiarism control used to write its plagiarism case post without an author. It now writes it
            in the name of a course instructor, and the posts it left behind get the same treatment: the instructor of
            the post's course with the lowest id. A post whose course has no instructor keeps its empty author, and the
            precondition on the next changeset then leaves the column as it is.
        </comment>
        <sql>
            UPDATE post SET author_id = (
                SELECT MIN(ucr.user_id)
                FROM user_course_role ucr
                    JOIN exercise e ON e.course_id = ucr.course_id
                    JOIN plagiarism_case pc ON pc.exercise_id = e.id
                WHERE pc.id = post.plagiarism_case_id
                    AND ucr.course_role = 'INSTRUCTOR'
            )
            WHERE author_id IS NULL AND plagiarism_case_id IS NOT NULL;
        </sql>
    </changeSet>
    <changeSet id="20260828100000-38-post-author-not-null" author="krusche">
